<h2 id="green">The Class's Real Testing Standout</h2>
<p>While the three quarterbacks debuting this preseason mostly skipped or downplayed testing, one passer in the same draft class put on a show that's worth knowing about for context: Arkansas's Taylen Green set multiple combine records for a quarterback, running a 4.36-second 40-yard dash, posting a 43.5-inch vertical jump, and recording an 11-foot-2 broad jump — all combine records for the position. Green's numbers illustrate just how wide the range of athletic profiles can be at quarterback in a single draft class, from Mendoza's pure size-and-processing build to Green's track-level explosiveness.</p>
